			"widgets_values":[
				"**subject_definitions:**\n\n`<Subject 1>` is 角色 A, a young East Asian woman whose facial appearance, hairstyle, and outfit come from `ref_images1.ref_image_0`: black hair pulled into a low ponytail with a few loose wispy strands framing her face, warm brown eyes, fair skin, a champagne-colored satin spaghetti-strap slip midi dress with a draped cowl neckline and fitted waist, a thin silver necklace with a textured heart-shaped pendant, and nude strappy stiletto heels. She is the teasing best friend.\n\n`<Subject 2>` is 角色 B, a young East Asian woman whose facial appearance, hairstyle, and outfit come from `ref_images2.ref_image_1`: shoulder-length smooth black hair with a soft inward curl at the ends, warm brown eyes, a yellow spaghetti-strap midi dress printed with small red roses and tiny green leaves, and beige low block-heel slide sandals. She holds a clear plastic cup of milk tea with black boba pearls.\n\nAll character dialogue is driven by `drive_audio`; every character's lip movements must be synchronized with the driving audio syllable by syllable (口型与驱动音频逐音节同步).\n\n**summary:**\n\n[reference generation] The target video is a 15-second lighthearted comedic scene set in a cozy milk tea shop on a warm afternoon. `<Subject 1>` teases `<Subject 2>` about her contradictory diet claim—she ordered sugar-free milk tea but still added boba pearls. The video alternates medium two-shots and close-ups of the two girlfriends across five dialogue beats. All lip movements are driven by `drive_audio` and synchronized with the driving audio syllable by syllable (口型与驱动音频逐音节同步).\n\n**retention_analysis:**\n\n`<Subject 1>` (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 3], [Shot 5]): fully_preserved — the low-ponytail black hair, champagne satin slip dress, silver heart pendant, and facial features from `ref_images1.ref_image_0` are retained.\n\n`<Subject 2>` (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2], [Shot 4]): fully_preserved — the shoulder-length wavy black hair, yellow rose-print dress, and facial features from `ref_images2.ref_image_1` are retained.\n\n**detailed_description:**\n\nThe target video uses a warm, realistic lifestyle vlog style with soft afternoon natural light filtering through large café windows, a gently shallow depth of field, and subtle hand-held camera breathing. The milk tea shop interior features light wooden round tables, pastel pink and cream wall panels, a backlit illuminated menu board on the wall, and faint bokeh of other patrons seated in the background. All character lip movements are driven by `drive_audio` and synchronized with the driving audio syllable by syllable (口型与驱动音频逐音节同步).\n\n[Shot 1] A medium two-shot frames `<Subject 1>` on the left and `<Subject 2>` on the right, seated across from each other at a small round wooden table. `<Subject 2>` holds a clear plastic cup of light-brown milk tea with chewy black boba pearls settled at the bottom, a straw piercing the lid, and raises it halfway to her lips, about to take a sip. `<Subject 1>`, in her champagne satin slip dress and silver heart pendant, turns her head toward `<Subject 2>`, her eyes narrowing playfully and one eyebrow lifting. `<Subject 1>` (S1) speaks in a light, teasing young female voice; her lips part to form each syllable in sync with `drive_audio`, her lower jaw dropping slightly on open vowels and her lips rounding on the final \"ao\", saying `<d>[中文] 你昨天不是说要减肥吗？</d>`. After the line, her lips close into an amused half-smile and she tilts her chin a fraction.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:03.500, the shot cuts to a close-up of `<Subject 2>`, the woman in the yellow rose-print dress. She lowers the milk tea cup slightly from her mouth and gives `<Subject 1>` a confident, unapologetic look, her chin lifting a fraction. `<Subject 2>` (S2) responds in a brighter, matter-of-fact young female voice; her mouth opens and closes with each syllable in sync with `drive_audio`, her upper teeth briefly visible as she says \"对\", her jaw moving naturally through the longer second phrase, saying `<d>[中文] 对啊，所以我把奶茶换成了无糖的。</d>`. She gives a small self-satisfied nod and taps the side of the cup with one fingertip.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:07.000, the shot cuts to a close-up of `<Subject 1>`, who glances pointedly down at the black boba pearls visible through the clear cup held off-screen, then back up at `<Subject 2>` with a knowing smirk. `<Subject 1>` (S1) asks; her lips purse slightly on the \"那\" initial and part cleanly with the question's rising intonation, her jaw moving lightly in sync with `drive_audio`, saying `<d>[中文] 那你还加珍珠？</d>`. Her eyebrows rise and she lets a soft breath through her nose.\n\n[Shot 4] At 00:09.000, the shot cuts to a close-up of `<Subject 2>`. She puffs her cheeks almost imperceptibly, then leans forward slightly and taps the boba pearls through the cup wall with a righteous expression. `<Subject 2>` (S2) retorts; her mouth stretches wide on the \"嚼\" vowel and her jaw drops emphatically on \"不算喝\", every syllable locked to `drive_audio`, saying `<d>[中文] 珍珠是嚼的，不算喝。</d>`. She seals her lips in a stubborn little pout and lifts the cup as if to defend it.\n\n[Shot 5] At 00:12.000, the shot cuts back to a medium two-shot of both women. `<Subject 1>` bursts out laughing, leaning back slightly and waving one hand dismissively, while `<Subject 2>` takes a quick sip through the straw with a guilty-but-smiling look. `<Subject 1>` (S1) laughs aloud, her mouth wide open in a natural laugh—lips retracted, jaw dropped, the corners of her eyes crinkling—then says through residual chuckles, her lips forming each syllable of `drive_audio`, `<d>[中文] 哈哈，有道理。</d>`. She shakes her head with a grin and raises her own empty cup in a mock toast. The frame holds on both of them smiling at each other.\n\n**overall_soundscape:**\n\nWarm milk tea shop ambient room tone continues throughout: a low hum of refrigerators and air conditioning, faint clinking of cups and spoons from the service counter, soft background chatter of other patrons at a distance, and a brief wet sucking sound of the straw drawing up boba pearls during the close-up of `<Subject 2>`'s drink.\n\n**non_diegetic_music:**\n\nA light, bouncy ukulele-and-whistle background track at a cheerful 110 BPM, entering softly under the first line, maintaining a playful comedic tone, and swelling slightly under the final laugh before fading out by the last frame."
